returned_finding_id	P1-execution-intake-bypass
returned_finding	intakeV7 implements the sealed outer authority check, but exported runV7({authority,evidenceRoot,runCommand}) directly accepts an arbitrary caller-supplied authority.target and invokes Docker/psql without calling intakeV7 or validating the four reviewed artifact SHAs. Consequently a Docker-capable caller can bypass the sealed outer authority by importing runV7 directly.
impact	The v6 fail-closed finding remains open at the executable boundary. The four-signature chain is a correct intended path but is not mandatory for execution.
required_correction	Make the only executable entry point invoke intakeV7 internally and keep the post-intake authority private/unforgeable; do not export or otherwise expose a target-accepting execution function. Add a regression test proving direct execution without the four immutable GO inputs causes zero child/Docker calls.

returned_finding_id_2	P2-unique-resource-self-attestation-only
returned_finding_2	The resource contract checks the new v7 naming pattern and prior_target_reuse=false field, but it has no immutable resource ledger or external inventory binding that proves the proposed runId, container full ID, database, and volume have never appeared in a prior candidate. A future authority can self-assert false while naming a previously used v7 resource.
impact_2	G/H and A-F namespace reuse is rejected structurally, but prior v7 resource/runId reuse is not independently fail-closed.
required_correction_2	Bind resource creation to an append-only immutable registry or a fresh inventory evidence artifact verified by the executor, covering runId, container ID/name, database, and volume ID; reject any previously recorded identity before Docker access.
status_after_review	NO-GO-for-resource-create-or-execute-until-P1-and-P2-are-corrected-and-fresh-DB-QA-DRAIN-RESOURCE-reviews-issue-GO
